WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.520
The sheet draws a sketch before thalamic axons arrive.

2
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.300
Does the sketch need those axons at all?

3
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:14.253
Start with a mouse that lacks the transcription factor Gbx2.

4
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:18.583
In these mice, thalamic axons never reach the cortex.

5
00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:24.507
If areas came only from thalamic input, what should the marker borders look like at

6
00:00:24.507 --> 00:00:25.487
birth?

7
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:32.877
They should be missing or misplaced.

8
00:00:33.957 --> 00:00:34.957
They were not.

9
00:00:35.517 --> 00:00:41.897
In 1999, Emily Miyashita-Lin, John Rubenstein and colleagues found normal borders

10
00:00:41.897 --> 00:00:43.677
for several area markers at birth.

11
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.300
The marker sketch forms without thalamic input.

12
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:49.803
The limit is the readout.

13
00:00:50.643 --> 00:00:54.283
Markers at birth are a sketch, and adult borders could still need input.

14
00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:56.783
Now ask the other question.

15
00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:58.683
What does input add?

16
00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:05.927
In 1991, Bradley Schlaggar and O'Leary grafted visual cortex from fetal rats into

17
00:01:05.927 --> 00:01:08.047
newborn rat somatosensory cortex.

18
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.930
Thalamic axons carrying whisker signals grew into the graft.

19
00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:14.810
What should the graft build?

20
00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:22.413
It formed barrels.

21
00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:27.913
Tissue that would have become visual cortex built a feature of the area whose input

22
00:01:27.913 --> 00:01:28.913
it received.

23
00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:34.527
Mriganka Sur's laboratory went further, in ferrets, which are born with immature

24
00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.527
visual pathways.

25
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:39.737
In newborns, the retina's normal targets were reduced.

26
00:01:40.677 --> 00:01:43.637
The normal inputs to the auditory thalamus were removed.

27
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:48.250
Retinal axons then grew into the auditory thalamus.

28
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.650
Auditory cortex received visual activity.

29
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:56.403
Normal auditory cortex has no map of edge orientation.

30
00:01:57.343 --> 00:01:58.943
What did the rewired cortex build?

31
00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:11.107
Neurons tuned to edge orientation, arranged in a map like visual cortex, though less

32
00:02:11.107 --> 00:02:12.107
regular.

33
00:02:12.517 --> 00:02:17.357
A companion paper reported that the animals responded to light through the rewired

34
00:02:17.357 --> 00:02:19.237
pathway as a visual stimulus.

35
00:02:20.317 --> 00:02:22.217
Input also sharpens the sketch.

36
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:29.610
In 2013, Shen-Ju Chou and colleagues in O'Leary's laboratory removed the axons from

37
00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.610
the visual thalamus.

38
00:02:31.533 --> 00:02:36.513
The genetic distinction between primary visual cortex and the higher-order areas

39
00:02:36.513 --> 00:02:38.213
around it failed to develop.

40
00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:43.983
Spontaneous and sensory activity then refine the maps inside each area.

41
00:02:45.043 --> 00:02:46.123
Later lessons take that up.

42
00:02:46.983 --> 00:02:50.543
The takeaway: the marker sketch forms without input by birth.

43
00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:54.243
Input then sharpens it, and shapes what each area builds.
